WEBVTT

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.610
<b>Minami Kamakura Girls Bicycle Club
 Miura Peninsula Touring Report</b>

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:13.610
Um...

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:15.450
What do you think?

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.410
It's very good.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.940
Without wasting any club funds,
you bought packing bags and went touring.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.290
You did very well.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.630
Right?

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.850
We worked really hard to come up with ideas

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.430
for how the bicycle club 
could produce results.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:34.540
Results, huh?

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.770
That's right. It wasn't just 
this touring trip, either.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.470
We raced in the Night Criterium, and, um...

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.020
We went orienteering, too.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.560
Our race against Azuma-senpai... 
doesn't really fit the bill.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.900
What do you think?

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.330
With all we've achieved,

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:53.820
surely you'll recognize the bicycle 
club as an official club now.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.200
Well...

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.510
I don't think I can.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.200
N-No way.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.560
Aren't you forgetting something?

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.220
What?

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.800
Forgetting something?

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.090
Are we?

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.960
Yes, something important.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:17.120
Something important?

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.980
Oh, come on!

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.830
What is this "important thing"?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:56.960
<b>#12  The Road Keeps Going</b>

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.510
What do you think it is?

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:57.570
I'm not sure.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.040
But the principal said...

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:04.030
That's something for you to think about.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.970
Remember?

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.180
Yeah, but...

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.250
I wish she'd given us a hint.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:12.670
Hot, hot!

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:15.950
What was that for? You surprised me.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.040
Is something wrong?

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.110
It's this.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.330
"Minami Kamakura High School Student Rules"?

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.900
Read this section.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.800
Let's see...

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.180
"Should students desire to form a new club,

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.790
they must gather at least five club members

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.270
and submit the designated 
application to the school."

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.030
What does it mean?

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:41.150
In other words, in order to form a new club,
we need at least five members.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.840
So what? There's five of us.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:45.920
That's right.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:52.500
There's me, Tomo-chan, Natsumi-chan, 
Fuyune-chan, and Sandy.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.790
Yes, me.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.480
Huh?

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.430
Something doesn't feel right.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:58.710
Right?

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:03.090
Give me a second.
I'll replay my mental video.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:10.140
I don't remember Sandy becoming a member.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.620
That's right.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:14.970
She temporarily joined the club 
during the orienteering activity,

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:17.670
and we haven't followed up 
on that since then.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.450
Y-You're right!

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:23.200
That's it! This must be the important 
thing my grandmother was talking about!

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.690
Wrong.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.620
We were wrong!

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.420
Maybe there's something missing 
from our achievements.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.460
Like what?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.080
Like distance?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.510
Maybe she's telling us 
to go on a longer tour.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.580
How long are we talking?

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.510
We rode 40 kilometers the other day.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.480
Then why don't we try for 100 kilometers?

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:48.600
100 kilometers?

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.330
I don't think we can ride that far in a day.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.730
Oh, maybe that's it.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.060
What?

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.460
An overnight trip.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.490
Maybe she's telling us to spend at 
least two days riding our bikes.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:03.440
Does that mean riding with tents?

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.400
Oh, like camping?

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.120
I don't like tents.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.190
Maybe we could stay at 
a youth hostel instead.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:14.080
They're cheap and all over the place.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:18.830
Come to think of it, the principal said 
she used to do that when she was younger.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.800
We can have a pillow fight!

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.910
<i>Something important, huh?</i>

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.680
Oh, it's already so late.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:35.140
I have something I need to do at home today.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.630
Should we call it a day, then?

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.590
I wish we could talk a little more.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.760
Then let's go somewhere else.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:47.560
The change of pace could 
inspire some good ideas.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:48.650
You're right.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.280
Is Flat okay?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.160
Yeah.

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:54.420
See you tomorrow.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:03.460
The problem is we don't know what this 
important thing the principal mentioned is.

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:06.840
It always comes back to that.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.600
It's an emergency, girls.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.760
Shiki-sensei?

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:16.680
What?

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.880
Sandy's going back to America?

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:22.150
Yeah. I just heard about it at school.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:24.480
Yeah, I know.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.150
I'm going home now and will pack my stuff.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.340
It's all right. I already
talked to the school.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:31.550
Sandy?

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:32.540
Tickets and everything's ready.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.080
Anyway, how's grandma doing?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.900
Is she eating? I'm so worried.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:37.790
She's talking about her grandmother.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:39.440
I heard she's lost a lot of weight.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.080
Don't worry. I'm okay.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.840
And I'm coming back real soon.

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:45.840
Sandy's grandmother...

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:49.800
She was supposed to stay for a year.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.780
It must be really bad if she's 
going home before her time's up.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.030
When is she going back?

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:58.240
I checked with her homeroom teacher.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:00.770
She's going to America next week.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:01.790
Next week?

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:04.310
Then when she said she had to go home...

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:06.910
She must be getting ready to go back.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:10.710
That's kind of standoffish, isn't it?

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:11.240
What?

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.240
Don't you think so?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.790
She could've at least mentioned it to us.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.580
I thought we were friends.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.170
Maybe it's because you're friends.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.770
What do you mean?

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.240
It must be hard for Sandy, too.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.390
Maybe she didn't mention it 
until the last minute

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:33.050
because she didn't want 
to make things gloomy.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:35.180
I see.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.140
Maybe.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.850
We knew she'd go back to 
America eventually, but...

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:51.280
Hey, let's make memories for Sandy in Japan.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.240
Memories?

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.160
What are you thinking?

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.430
Touring. Let's ride with Sandy.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.520
That's a good idea.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:04.540
It's a good way for us to send her off.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.500
But where will we go?

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:11.220
We know a place that's perfect for Sandy.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.720
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.600
We're going to bike up Mt. Fuji?

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.340
Yeah.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:21.100
Not to the peak, though.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:25.290
There's a road called the Mt. Fuji Skyline 
that goes up to the fifth station.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.150
Although riding to the fifth 
station would be tough for us.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.980
After all, it's 2,400 meters above sea level.

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:34.140
Wow.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.570
We were planning to travel to Gotenba,

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.620
but even then we'd have
 to climb close to 2,000 meters.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:43.090
So our destination this time 
will be the second station.

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:48.590
That's still a twenty-five-kilometer course 
ending at 1,600 meters above sea level.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:51.090
That's about one mile.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:56.230
There are a few parking areas 
along the Mt. Fuji Skyline,

00:08:56.230 --> 00:09:00.280
so we're asking Shiki-sensei to drive along.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:03.120
We'll be covered even if we drop out partway.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.350
What do you think? You'll come, right, Sandy?

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:06.940
Of course.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:11.410
Then let's meet next Sunday 
at 7:00 AM at Kamakura Station.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:15.030
Okay. I'm excited to go to Mt. Fuji.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:19.030
We made it to Gotenba.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:23.260
It's already 9:30 AM, so I guess 
we'll be leaving at 10:00 AM.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:25.830
It seems so close,
since we see it all the time,

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.670
but Mt. Fuji's actually pretty far away.

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:33.640
Wow! Mt. Fuji looks huge.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:37.050
Hey, there's still snow on the top.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:41.690
Of course. It's 3,776 meters above sea level.

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:44.350
According to the Köppen climate 
classification we studied in geography,

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.060
it's a tundra at the summit.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.520
Tundra?

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:52.670
Even during the summer, the lowest 
temperatures can reach below freezing.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:55.190
Mt. Fuji is not to be underestimated.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.060
Girls.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.910
It's huge. What is this car, a bus?

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.830
It's a camping car.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.610
Nice, right? We rented it.

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:09.830
We'll support you today using this car.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.810
Thank you.

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:14.800
The two of them aren't the 
only ones providing support.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:16.430
The manager?

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:20.430
Indeed. I am Hooji Korone, 
Manager of Cycle Flat.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.300
<b>Closed</b>

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:28.140
Today's course is all uphill.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:31.180
It may be short, but brace yourselves.

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:32.110
Okay.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:37.680
Let's head for Mt. Fuji.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:39.280
Yeah!

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:42.160
America, huh?

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.180
That's really far away 
for a high school girl.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:49.120
Make some good memories, girls.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:52.460
First, we'll be riding through 
the city of Gotenba.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:57.260
The hills are pretty gentle here, 
so think of it as a warm up.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.430
Roger that.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.430
Okay.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:09.250
Wow, Mt. Fuji's right in front of us.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:16.180
Once we pass the Self-Defense Force
drill field, it'll start getting steeper.

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:16.780
Yikes.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.030
Wow.

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:09.380
This is the old toll booth, huh?

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:12.710
Until about twenty years ago, 
this was a toll road.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.710
It's a place where noble 
soldiers once dreamed a dream.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.840
That means something totally different.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:20.970
Tomo-chan, how much farther are we riding?

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:24.950
Well, it's about three kilometers 
to the second station.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.850
We'll be climbing about 150 meters.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.010
We're almost there.

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:32.640
Shall we go, then?

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.610
H-Hey, don't you think we're going too fast?

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:53.700
Yeah. Fuyune-san can't keep up.

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:56.580
Sandy, let's go a little slower.

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:58.040
No.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.040
What?

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:03.350
I'm excited. This is where the battle begins.

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:07.720
Let's race to see who reaches 
the second station first.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:08.780
What?

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:11.600
I accept your challenge!

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:17.290
If you don't hurry, I'll leave you behind!

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:18.940
You won't beat me!

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:22.180
They're full of energy.

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:24.290
In that case...

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:25.970
Let's race, too.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.200
Yeah.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:45.630
<b>Elevation</b>

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:45.630
<b>Feeling Great!
Mt. Fuji</b>

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:45.630
<b>Second Station</b>

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:53.880
They're here.

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:57.240
Hey, seems like they've turned it into a race.

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:59.980
They're hopeless.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:01.700
But...

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:02.680
Yeah.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.780
It's the last spurt!

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:12.580
They seem to be having fun.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:15.040
Goal!

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:17.630
I lost.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:18.880
We made it.

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:21.080
That was tough.

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:26.600
Sandy, you really are fast.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:28.800
Your power's on a different level.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:31.550
No, you were all very fast.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:35.430
Even though I rode as hard as I could, 
you kept up with me until the end.

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:37.640
Now that you mention it, you're right.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.650
We dropped out so early during the criterium.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.530
Have we...

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:46.780
Gotten faster?

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.390
Good work, everyone.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:51.490
Have some cold water.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.640
Thank you.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:15:08.340
<b>Second Station</b>

00:14:54.580 --> 00:15:08.340
<b>Elevation</b>

00:14:54.580 --> 00:15:08.340
<b>Feeling Great!
Mt. Fuji</b>

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:58.970
We're at 1,600 meters.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:02.240
I can't believe we really came here.

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:05.170
Two horizontal lines form 
the character for "two."

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:08.340
We're still only at two out of ten.

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:10.100
Sandy?

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:12.800
Someday, I'll ride my bicycle to the fifth...

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:15.760
No, the tenth station.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:18.340
I'd like to go to the peak.

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:20.810
Yeah. Wait, the peak?

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.730
That's not possible.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:25.320
But...

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:31.280
It would be nice if we 
could go together someday.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:34.780
I'm sure we will someday.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.770
Hiromi?

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:38.700
But Sandy...

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.710
Sandy, you're...

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.330
Wh-What's wrong, Hiromi?

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:46.030
Does your stomach hurt?

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:49.630
Sandy, do you like riding your bike?

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:53.510
You'll keep riding even after 
you go back to America, right?

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:55.180
Of course.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:59.830
You taught me how fun 
bicycles can be in Japan.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:02.420
Good. Then we'll be fine.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.480
Did you know?

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:10.440
You can go anywhere in the world on a bike.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.230
You're right.

00:16:12.230 --> 00:16:14.070
As long as we keep riding...

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:15.780
Someday...

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.550
We'll meet again.

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:21.860
Let's not cry anymore.

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:25.950
Bicycles are fun. Tears don't suit them.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.270
You're right.

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:29.890
Let's smile...

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.300
As we send off Sandy.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.800
Well done.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.490
Grandmother, what are you doing here?

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:42.390
I heard about your touring 
trip from Shiki-sensei.

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:46.100
I came here on my bicycle when I was young.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.230
Getting old is no fun.

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:52.410
That's not what I meant. 
Why did you come here?

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:54.860
And what do you mean by "well done"?

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:59.620
You've realized what's 
important, haven't you?

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.080
What?

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:08.500
The most important thing is 
to enjoy riding your bicycles.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:10.980
The important thing...

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:12.760
It was that simple?

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:15.510
Simple? Are you sure?

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:20.350
We were working hard to get 
the bicycle club recognized.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:25.220
But actually enjoying our bicycles 
might've taken a backseat to that.

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:27.310
But if you'd just told us—

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:29.880
No, I couldn't do that.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:34.490
You had to realize your 
enjoyment on your own.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:38.450
And you did it.

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:45.830
So I'm officially recognizing the 
Minami Kamakura Girls' Bicycle Club.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:46.570
We...

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:48.710
We did it!

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:53.420
It was a long road.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.380
But we were finally recognized.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.180
That's great.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:02.890
We finally formed the bicycle club,
but now we have to say goodbye to Sandy.

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:06.350
Um, what are you talking about?

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.060
Sorry, Sandy. We heard the news.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:12.160
We know you were trying to hide it, but...

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:13.800
You're going home, right?

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.430
You knew?

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:19.330
We understand how you feel, 
but you could've told us.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:23.450
Sorry, but I didn't think 
it was worth reporting.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.700
What are you talking about?

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.250
You're going back to America, right?

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:30.730
Yes, for just one week.

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:33.500
One week?

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.760
Just one week?

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:37.630
Just one.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:40.310
But your grandmother's not doing well.

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:44.400
Yes. She's feeling down 
because she misses me.

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:45.550
She's not sick?

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:48.290
No, she's healthy otherwise.

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:55.540
B-But she was talking about
"grandma" and "loss," so I thought...

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:56.780
Sensei!

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:01.450
Sorry! I've always been bad at English.

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:07.180
So Shiki-sensei was just confused.

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:09.960
But I'm glad Sandy's not leaving us.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.170
Yeah.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.160
Yeah!

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:14.340
Hey, girls.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:16.210
What?

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:19.170
Why don't we ride a little farther?

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:20.030
What?

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:22.550
After all, the road keeps going.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:23.990
See?

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.560
Let's go.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:32.380
Sure. We'll follow you as far 
as you want to go, Hiromi.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:33.560
Yeah, let's go.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:38.140
This is the bicycle club's 
first tour as an official club.

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:39.650
Sandy, are you coming with us?

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.530
Yes, of course.

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:47.680
<i>Yes, the road keeps going.</i>

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.610
<i>So let's go, Unico.</i>

00:19:54.030 --> 00:20:00.520
<i>With Tomo-chan, Fuyune-chan, Natsumi-chan, 
Sandy, and everyone else.</i>

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:08.890
<i>Let's ride far, far away to see 
sights we've never seen before.</i>

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:45.250
<i>The appeal of road bikes on full display 
makes you want to start riding tomorrow.</i>

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:48.200
<i>A-O-P: The first cycling club.</i>

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:55.080
<b>Kamakura Cycling</b>

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:55.080
<b>Enoshima</b>

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:55.080
<b>Shichirigahama</b>

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:55.080
<b>Inamuragasaki</b>

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:55.080
<b>Enoshima Line</b>

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:55.080
<b>Kamakura Station</b>

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:55.080
<b>Yokosuka Line</b>

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:52.200
<i>We're heading for Enoshima while 
making stops along the way</i>

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.230
<i>in our first cycling tour of Kamakura.</i>

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.650
<i>Last time we stopped at a popular scenic spot</i>

00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:01.160
<i>and enjoyed a famous rice bowl in Enoshima.</i>

00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:04.190
<i>This time we'll be heading for...</i>

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:08.350
Now that we're full...

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.350
Yeah, that was good.

00:22:08.350 --> 00:22:11.460
We're going to be finishing in Inamuragasaki.

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:15.800
<i>Our first Kamakura cycling 
experience is in its final stage.</i>

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:18.940
<b>Enoshima</b>

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:18.940
<b>Shichirigahama</b>

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:18.940
<b>Inamuragasaki</b>

00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:18.130
<i>We're heading for Inamuragasaki, 
our final destination.</i>

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:21.830
Enoshima was fun.

00:22:21.830 --> 00:22:23.570
It sure was.

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:27.260
We're leaving Enoshima.

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:28.700
Farewell.

00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:41.810
* Filmed on pedestrian path

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:40.980
<i>That went by in a flash.</i>

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:44.390
<i>Riding a road bike, riding through Kamakura,</i>

00:22:44.390 --> 00:22:50.240
<i>and everything else was a new experience, 
but we had no idea it was so much fun.</i>

00:22:55.790 --> 00:22:57.780
<i>When we rode alongside the Enoshima train,</i>

00:22:57.780 --> 00:23:01.510
<i>it was exciting, like a scene out of an anime.</i>

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:11.670
We've arrived at Inamuragasaki.

00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:15.410
<b>Inamuragasaki</b>

00:23:09.970 --> 00:23:12.070
All right.

00:23:12.590 --> 00:23:14.990
<i>We got to experience some 
great things like</i>

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:17.770
<i>the spectacular views of Kamakura and cycling.</i>

00:23:19.100 --> 00:23:21.210
How do you feel about today?

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:26.030
It was my first time riding a
road bike, but I had a lot of fun.

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:31.010
Yeah. You can go all over the 
place so quickly on a road bike,

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:33.330
so we got to enjoy a bunch of 
different places in one day.

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:38.020
Why don't you give road bikes a try?

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:38.760
Yeah.
